{"title":"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> that can be represented as repeating <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Decimal\" title=\"Decimal\"> decimals</a> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e58505a03d4aa6fc9edcaf2145ec4c538e1b6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{abc}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Digit\" title=\"Digit\">digits</a>. Find the sum of the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e070383e926439d2af0a58994af4e2782364c8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Numbers of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e58505a03d4aa6fc9edcaf2145ec4c538e1b6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{abc}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/92199e562c4510885c3fe965a12415a628371f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{abc}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7fdb7c7777b06d3361261ab278606c9cba3516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\times9\\times8=720$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> such numbers. Each digit will appear in each place value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e5d624d79420d51578b6267dca7dfb4b419b8e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{720}{10}=72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" /> times, and the sum of the digits, 0 through 9, is 45. So the sum of all the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc885f0284b9c2252ccccabd0269d098bdd18fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45\\times72\\times111}{999}= \\boxed{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, for every number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e58505a03d4aa6fc9edcaf2145ec4c538e1b6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{abc}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />, there will be exactly one other number, such that when they are added together, the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53e84105b9ba7b81a39447aa2e403fe6636328a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{999}$\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, or, more precisely, 1. As an example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd205d621a211c01d5c2fe3f713b7873d6c450f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.\\overline{123}+.\\overline{876}=.\\overline{999} \\Longrightarrow 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the solution can be determined by dividing the total number of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Permutation\" title=\"Permutation\">permutations</a> by 2. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9edf82dff7968237a534c72e76268a8fdb3b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 8}{2} = \\frac{720}{2}= \\boxed{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Another method, albeit a little risky, that can be used is to note that the numbers between 1 and 999 with distinct digits average out to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9ee37977654ae82a2231be5274cdbf709d15d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{999}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. Then the total sum becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80ccd8946420a3cf06aa43d882ecdd889edea37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{999}{2}\\times720}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" /> which reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/7597c3975a70e5bd0b0413b6abf3dee9d6126999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way is to do complementary counting and casework. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f6606b4e60bb892a33829665efaef6922bc69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{abc} = abc/999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"23\" />. Excluding numbers with repeating digits our answer would just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05decb77d959fcd8ef16ff9131926372fb039b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{999 \\cdot (1000/2)}{999} = 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"40\" />. We subtract off the sum of the numbers with at least two digits being the same:\n</p><p><br />\nCase 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4562767217eaa6e7acb7b2d04cfc167404e8a282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$aba$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />: Sum = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d37a7f187200d0a223de781a21ff42893c8330f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1010(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 9) + 450\\cdot 10 = 999 \\cdot 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"362\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18e0aa8c28a3c5ff5e89f47a6a0078a7338a55d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$aab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />: Sum = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3bc1717c1d9bc944fd9eb796a2652962c155f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1100(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 9) + 45\\cdot 10 = 999 \\cdot 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"353\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nCase 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b99ab3f921ba04ff2dd0986253759f1bc3ab31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$baa$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />: Sum = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/70512c1befacf7524b004a7a3f48e5ad422ae891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 9) + 4500\\cdot 10 = 999 \\cdot 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"362\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe overcounted the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> <b>twice</b> (the numbers with all 3 digits being the same). The sum of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e22f6433e52623276b989300bd022767f9b6bb17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 9) = 999 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nSo, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f35dd352961bae2f0a3cc7478df7319de85058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{999 \\cdot 500 - 999 \\cdot 150 + 999 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 2}{999} = \\boxed{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"320\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I\" title=\"2006 AIME I\">2006 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https:/